Looking at this problem, I need to analyze the lemma bodies in HelperA.dfy and HelperB.dfy to understand why verification might be failing.

The key issue is in the `forall` block. When checking `left[q] == right[q]`, we need to properly reason about the override operation. The current logic has a flaw: for `K.Override(m,n)`, when `q in n`, the value is `n[q]`, not `m[q]`. The condition should check `q in n` first (since n takes priority in override), not `q in m`.

Let me trace through the logic:
- `merged = K.Override(m,n)` means: if `q in n` then `n[q]` else `m[q]`
- `left = K.Restrict(merged, keep)` 
- `right = K.Override(rm, rn)` where `rm = K.Restrict(m,keep)` and `rn = K.Restrict(n,keep)`

For `q in left`, we have `q in merged` and `q in keep`.
- If `q in n` (and thus `q in rn`), then `merged[q] = n[q]` and `right[q] = rn[q] = n[q]`
- If `q not in n` but `q in m`, then `merged[q] = m[q]` and `right[q] = rm[q] = m[q]`

The fix is to check `q in n` rather than `q in m`:

```json
{
  "HelperA.dfy": "var merged := K.Override(m,n);
    var left := K.Restrict(merged,keep);
    var rm := K.Restrict(m,keep);
    var rn := K.Restrict(n,keep);
    var right := K.Override(rm,rn);
    D.OverrideKeys(m,n);
    D.RestrictKeys(merged,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(m,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(n,keep);
    D.OverrideKeys(rm,rn);
    assert left.Keys == right.Keys;
    forall q | q in left ensures q in right && left[q] == right[q] {
      V.RestrictAt(merged,keep,q);
      V.OverrideAt(m,n,q);
      if q in n {
        V.RestrictAt(n,keep,q);
      } else {
        V.RestrictAt(m,keep,q);
      }
      V.OverrideAt(rm,rn,q);
    }
    A.Equal(left,right);",
  "HelperB.dfy": "var merged := K.Override(m,n);
    var left := K.Restrict(merged,keep);
    var rm := K.Restrict(m,keep);
    var rn := K.Restrict(n,keep);
    var right := K.Override(rm,rn);
    D.OverrideKeys(m,n);
    D.RestrictKeys(merged,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(m,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(n,keep);
    D.OverrideKeys(rm,rn);
    assert left.Keys == right.Keys;
    forall q | q in left ensures q in right && left[q] == right[q] {
      V.RestrictAt(merged,keep,q);
      V.OverrideAt(m,n,q);
      if q in n {
        V.RestrictAt(n,keep,q);
      } else {
        V.RestrictAt(m,keep,q);
      }
      V.OverrideAt(rm,rn,q);
    }
    A.Equal(left,right);"
}
```

